# File and Directory Naming

Match the ecosystem and existing files in the same folder. Prefer one convention per file type in a given directory.

## React / TypeScript (`src/app/`)

- **PascalCase** for components and project pages: `Hero.tsx`, `WalkabilityIndex.tsx`, `App.tsx`
- **kebab-case** for UI primitives (shadcn-style): `toggle-group.tsx`, `scroll-area.tsx`
- Legacy lowercase (e.g. `footer.tsx`) exists; prefer PascalCase for new components
- Hooks/utils: camelCase or kebab (`use-mobile.ts`, `utils.ts`)
- Config/entry: lowercase when conventional (`main.tsx`, `setup.ts`)
- Directories: camelCase or lowercase (`app/`, `components/`, `projects/`)

## Assets (`public/`)

- **snake_case** filenames: `embodied_ai_compressed.gltf`, `og-default.jpg`
- Version suffixes: `header_v2.jpg`; thumbnails: `project_name_thumbnail.png`
- Directories: lowercase or snake_case (`assets/rhino/compressed/`)

## Docs

- snake_case for dirs and non-date files: `dev_notes/`, `session-management-best-practices.md`
- Date-prefixed sessions: `YYYY-MM-DD-[type]-[description].md` (e.g. `2026-02-12-refactor-portfolio-grid.md`)

## Avoid

- Mixing conventions in the same layer (don't add `ContactMe.tsx` next to `footer.tsx` without aligning)
- Renaming third-party or generated files
- PascalCase for non-component modules unless the folder already does

| Context | Convention | Examples |
|---------|------------|----------|
| React components | PascalCase | `App.tsx`, `Hero.tsx` |
| UI primitives | kebab-case | `toggle-group.tsx` |
| Hooks / utils | camelCase or kebab | `use-mobile.ts` |
| Asset filenames | snake_case | `embodied_ai.png` |
| Doc/session files | snake_case or date | `2026-02-12-refactor.md` |
| Directories | lowercase / snake_case | `src/app/`, `public/assets/rhino/` |
